1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,170
Why you?

3
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,590
How did you...

4
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:22,930
Ma'am.

5
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:24,690
Ma'am, can you hear me?

6
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:38,860
Ms. Hsieh!

7
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:45,020
What are you doing?

8
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:46,070
Are you saving this person?

9
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:47,000
I...

10
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,360
Do you know him?

11
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:49,289
No, I don't.

12
00:01:49,370 --> 00:01:51,880
Why do you want to save
someone you don't know?

13
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:52,850
I'm just trying to help.

14
00:01:52,979 --> 00:01:54,170
You're just trying to help?

15
00:01:54,259 --> 00:01:55,530
When I begged you to save my husband

16
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:56,500
and my son,

17
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:57,650
why didn't you help?

18
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,270
Why didn't you help my family?

19
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:00,420
But now, you're saving a stranger?

20
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:01,390
Answer me!

21
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:02,270
Who are you to decide

22
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:03,940
whether someone gets to live or not?

23
00:02:04,030 --> 00:02:05,830
Why didn't you save my husband

24
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,190
and my son when I begged you?

25
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:08,430
But now, you choose to save a stranger?

26
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,100
Answer me!

27
00:02:10,229 --> 00:02:12,520
Tell me who you are!

28
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,700
Do you also think

29
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:38,960
that I did the wrong thing?

30
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,730
This has nothing to do
with right or wrong.

31
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,940
You just did what you wanted.

32
00:02:45,079 --> 00:02:46,750
You saved the people you wanted to save.

33
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:50,180
I did save the people I wanted to save.

34
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,840
But she was right.

35
00:02:58,190 --> 00:02:59,730
Who do I think I am?

36
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,410
Why do I get to decide

37
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:09,140
who lives

38
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:12,400
and who dies?

39
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,510
I thought I'd be happy

40
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:20,050
if I could save lives.

41
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,230
But that's not true at all.

42
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,680
Because...

43
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:33,780
when I'm choosing whom to save

44
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:35,320
and who gets to live,

45
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:40,600
at the same time, I feel like I'm deciding

46
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,370
the fate of other people.

47
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,640
I really don't know

48
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:50,190
what Kakarayan wants me to do.

49
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,640
If He didn't want me to save people,

50
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:56,840
He wouldn't have given me this ability.

51
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:59,300
But He gave me this ability.

52
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:01,280
And now,

53
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:04,010
why is this happening to me?

54
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:06,600
If you want to know

55
00:04:06,690 --> 00:04:07,920
why Kakarayan did so,

56
00:04:08,010 --> 00:04:09,420
there's a quick way to find out.

57
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,160
And it is to use the Reflection of Time.

58
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:15,270
Reflection of Time?

59
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,240
Yes.

60
00:04:16,370 --> 00:04:17,250
Isn't the Reflection of Time

61
00:04:17,339 --> 00:04:19,100
the future Kakarayan has arranged?

62
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:22,660
I'm not the messenger though.

63
00:04:23,370 --> 00:04:27,280
The Reflection of Time is meant
for the messenger to see.

64
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,660
Are you saying that I can ask Kakarayan

65
00:04:29,750 --> 00:04:31,770
to let me see the Reflection of Time?

66
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:35,950
To be honest with you,
aside from the doomsday,

67
00:04:36,390 --> 00:04:37,140
I can no longer see

68
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:39,510
anything else in the Reflection of Time.

69
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,070
'Orad might not be able to see it.

70
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,440
But based on previous experience,

71
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:45,850
you managed to get in touch with Kakarayan

72
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:47,700
through the Ceremony of Connection, right?

73
00:04:48,230 --> 00:04:49,550
Furthermore,

74
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:51,880
you saw the Reflection of Time
that He wanted you to see.

75
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:55,050
So...

76
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:57,420
if you want to know what the future holds,

77
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:58,350
you're the only person

78
00:04:58,430 --> 00:05:00,060
who has the best chance to find out.

79
00:05:00,850 --> 00:05:10,450
♫ Show yourself before me ♫

80
00:05:17,350 --> 00:05:18,410
Kakarayan.

81
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,510
What do you want me to do?

82
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,710
Please tell me.

83
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:56,420
Don't you get it?

84
00:05:56,510 --> 00:05:59,280
The Reflection of Time itself is a curse.

85
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,260
[Give me the Comb of Memories.]

86
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:06,630
I remember now.

87
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:14,950
I remember everything.

88
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,150
Tien-ti.

89
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,340
Can you hear me?

90
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:38,790
Tien-ti!

91
00:06:41,870 --> 00:06:42,970
Tien-ti.

92
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:53,310
Please get in the car.

93
00:07:05,590 --> 00:07:07,520
From the moment you see the future,

94
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:09,640
you've already lost your future.

95
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:12,500
[From the very beginning,]

96
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:17,290
you were just a lie

97
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:20,150
that Kakarayan had made up

98
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,750
to make up for His regret.

99
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,620
'Orad!

100
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:35,950
What is it? What did you see?

101
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,220
Right, what did you see?

102
00:07:37,310 --> 00:07:38,760
Why were you so startled?

103
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:41,180
I saw you.

104
00:07:41,270 --> 00:07:41,840
Me?

105
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:42,770
You...

106
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:43,340
I...

107
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:45,320
I wasn't doing anything weird, was I?

108
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:46,680
I don't know how to describe it.

109
00:07:46,810 --> 00:07:48,790
There was a very big house.

110
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:50,600
But there was nothing inside.

111
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:54,600
Then a door suddenly appeared.

112
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:56,450
You walked past me,

113
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:59,130
pushed the door open, and walked in.

114
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:00,980
That's it?

115
00:08:01,330 --> 00:08:02,430
Did you see anything else?

116
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,020
If you only saw me

117
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:05,340
passing by you,

118
00:08:05,470 --> 00:08:07,140
I doubt it would've shocked you so badly.

119
00:08:07,230 --> 00:08:08,510
Then I saw...

120
00:08:10,570 --> 00:08:12,330
I think it was the car accident

121
00:08:13,650 --> 00:08:16,120
my parents were in when I was little.

122
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:18,140
Hold on.

123
00:08:18,890 --> 00:08:20,430
Are you saying
that you went back to the past

124
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,010
in a Reflection of Time of the future?

125
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,300
What's that about?

126
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:25,840
I don't know.

127
00:08:25,930 --> 00:08:26,990
What else did you see?

128
00:08:28,130 --> 00:08:28,480
That's right.

129
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:29,710
-What else did you see?
-I also...

130
00:08:32,789 --> 00:08:33,890
What?

131
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,520
[Don't you get it?]

132
00:08:35,650 --> 00:08:38,600
The Reflection of Time itself is a curse.

133
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,360
It's nothing.

134
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,570
Nothing? That's all?

135
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:55,720
It can't be.

136
00:08:56,330 --> 00:08:57,170
You should at least describe

137
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,490
how the house looked like,

138
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:00,380
why the door appeared there,

139
00:09:00,510 --> 00:09:01,610
and the part where you went back

140
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,060
to the car accident that happened
when you were little.

141
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,380
Let's call it a day.

142
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,660
But we need to get this straight.

143
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:06,580
The Reflection of Time she saw

144
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,730
might not even be true.

145
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:08,780
Let her rest.

146
00:09:09,930 --> 00:09:11,030
Take a rest, little girl.

147
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:12,350
Calm down.

148
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,760
I'll calm down too.

149
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:14,720
Okay, it's fine.

150
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:16,530
A big house with nothing in it.

151
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,730
I walked through a door.

152
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:21,720
I'll take you home first.

153
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:31,490
A big empty house.

154
00:09:31,710 --> 00:09:33,420
Then a door suddenly appeared

155
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,360
and I walked in.

156
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:38,480
A big empty house.

157
00:09:38,610 --> 00:09:39,450
Then a door suddenly appeared

158
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:40,510
and I walked in.

159
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,050
No.

160
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:43,810
Why did Kakarayan let her see

161
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:45,520
such Reflection of Time?

162
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:47,900
Why did I go to a big empty house

163
00:09:48,470 --> 00:09:50,850
without any reason?

164
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:53,490
I went through a door.

165
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:55,600
Did I go through the door
to look for something?

166
00:09:56,570 --> 00:09:59,030
Was I looking for someone or something?

167
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:01,890
This is annoying.

168
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,140
Darn it.

169
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:06,900
What the...

170
00:10:07,830 --> 00:10:09,370
This stupid thing.

171
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,820
Honey.

172
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:22,440
I must have gone

173
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,760
to that big empty house

174
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:25,340
because of you.

175
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:26,180
Am I right?

176
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,380
Answer me.

177
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:31,810
Don't look so stern.

178
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,130
Why won't you talk to me?

179
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:33,220
[Emptiness]

180
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:38,280
This was on your birthday in 2003.

181
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:43,070
This was

182
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:44,700
in 1999.

183
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:49,800
This was also in 1999.

184
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,440
It was in 1999.

185
00:10:56,710 --> 00:10:57,810
In 1999...

186
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:03,660
This was in 2009.

187
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:05,820
This was in 2002.

188
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:08,110
This was in 2008.

189
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:16,200
[November 27th, 1999, Mr. Li Pu-hui,
hired as a philosophy professor]

190
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,800
Isn't that the year
Tien-ti got into the car accident?

191
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:32,440
What's wrong?

192
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:40,140
It's nothing.

193
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:43,660
I'm just a bit tired

194
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,380
from what happened today.

195
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,970
Get some rest. I'll get going.

196
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,550
Whatever you saw
in the Reflection of Time,

197
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:09,700
don't be scared.

198
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:14,980
I'll always be by your side
to protect you.

199
00:12:16,130 --> 00:12:17,230
[I remember now.]

200
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:19,300
I remember everything.

201
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:21,540
From the very beginning,

202
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:23,430
you were just a lie

203
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:25,280
that Kakarayan had made up

204
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:26,910
to make up for His regret.

205
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:30,030
Don't be afraid, okay?

206
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,650
Get some rest.

207
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:46,490
I believe it.

208
00:12:47,590 --> 00:12:49,570
No matter what happens,

209
00:12:49,650 --> 00:12:51,370
you'll always be by my side.

210
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:53,970
You'll protect me.

211
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:57,840
You won't leave me.

212
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,350
I'll stay by your side and protect you.

213
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:06,810
I won't leave you.

214
00:13:47,690 --> 00:13:48,570
That's strange.

215
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:52,700
Why was the Reflection of Time she saw

216
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,730
different from what I saw?

217
00:14:01,850 --> 00:14:04,010
Li Pu-hui walked through a door.

218
00:14:05,370 --> 00:14:06,250
A door.

219
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,570
Is it the Cause and Effect
Correction Bureau?

220
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,250
No, it can't be.

221
00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:22,930
[Fali took you to see Kakarayan?]

222
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:26,450
Yes. He told me

223
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:29,440
that I'd be able to meet Kakarayan

224
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,860
if I went through the door.

225
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:36,610
Then what happened?

226
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:40,570
When I was about to walk
through that door,

227
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:42,420
you suddenly held my hand

228
00:14:42,550 --> 00:14:44,180
and told me not to go any further.

229
00:14:44,310 --> 00:14:45,850
Then I realized

230
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:49,990
the door that was supposed
to lead to Kakarayan

231
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:53,020
turned into the place
that you told me about.

232
00:14:53,110 --> 00:14:55,270
The place where the dead go.

233
00:14:56,810 --> 00:14:57,950
There's no way.

234
00:14:58,610 --> 00:14:59,360
Li Pu-hui!

235
00:15:01,470 --> 00:15:02,180
Li Pu-hui...

236
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,410
You wanted to see me?

237
00:16:13,410 --> 00:16:14,250
Let me ask you.

238
00:16:15,170 --> 00:16:16,660
The order to evacuate all Kawas

239
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:17,810
and return to Pinokayan,

240
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,540
was that Kakarayan's arrangement?

241
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,340
Or was it yours?

242
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,070
'Orad told me

243
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:27,090
that the last Reflection of Time he saw

244
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:28,410
stopped at the doomsday.

245
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,450
But before that, he saw

246
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:34,880
Hsieh Tien-ti dying in front of him.

247
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:36,640
Then he'd walk through that door

248
00:16:36,730 --> 00:16:38,000
that led to Pinokayan.

249
00:16:38,710 --> 00:16:40,600
If 'Orad had gone back to Pinokayan,

250
00:16:41,350 --> 00:16:42,930
that would mean
he would no longer be the messenger

251
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:44,300
Kakarayan appointed in this world.

252
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:47,020
Then how could he have known

253
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:50,190
that after the car accident,

254
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:52,440
Hsieh Tien-ti would donate her heart
to someone else?

255
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:54,900
And how would he know

256
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:56,750
what the world would become

257
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,020
after all the Kawas had left?

258
00:17:00,530 --> 00:17:02,770
The only possible answer to all this

259
00:17:03,570 --> 00:17:05,190
is that the Reflection of Time
that 'Orad saw

260
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,569
and the order to evacuate the Kawas

261
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:09,020
were your doing.

262
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,030
What is your motive

263
00:17:13,109 --> 00:17:14,569
behind it all?

264
00:17:15,619 --> 00:17:17,380
Does Pinokayan actually exist?

265
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:19,710
Where is my wife?

266
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:20,770
What about the other Kawas?

267
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,089
Where did they all go?

268
00:17:25,569 --> 00:17:26,890
The things you just said,

269
00:17:28,030 --> 00:17:29,440
have you told 'Orad about them?

270
00:17:31,290 --> 00:17:31,950
No.

271
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:34,760
Why?

272
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:39,030
Because I know

273
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,270
that if I had told him about this,

274
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,230
you would never tell the truth.

275
00:17:47,350 --> 00:17:48,660
So you came here

276
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:50,200
because you wanted

277
00:17:50,290 --> 00:17:51,960
to find out the whole truth?

278
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,600
You really are the god of wisdom,

279
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:59,270
wanting to know the real motive
behind everyone's actions

280
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:01,730
and explore the so-called truth.

281
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:05,870
I guess
that's more important than anything.

282
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:08,290
Don't assume that you know everything.

283
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:10,880
I don't care about the truth,

284
00:18:10,970 --> 00:18:12,820
nor am I interested in your plans.

285
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,640
I just want to know where my wife is.

286
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,000
Give me back my wife.

287
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:26,940
Do you want to see her?

288
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:28,700
Yes.

289
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:42,910
Then...

290
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:47,400
go and look for her.

291
00:19:01,170 --> 00:19:03,070
Then a door suddenly appeared.

292
00:19:03,730 --> 00:19:05,530
You walked past me,

293
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:08,740
pushed the door open, and walked in.

294
00:19:08,830 --> 00:19:12,480
So the Reflection of Time that Tien-ti saw

295
00:19:14,590 --> 00:19:15,690
was this moment.

296
00:19:55,160 --> 00:20:04,530
♫ Show yourself before me ♫

297
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:09,720
Please appear before me,

298
00:20:11,790 --> 00:20:14,250
the Kariah that symbolizes lies,

299
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,250
Toem.

300
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,940
[Li Pu-hui, where is your necklace?]

301
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,530
I think I lost it.

302
00:21:10,790 --> 00:21:12,020
It's such an important thing.

303
00:21:12,110 --> 00:21:14,000
The necklace symbolizes that we're Kawas.

304
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:16,470
[It's a promise between us and Kakarayan.]

305
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,020
[How could you lose
something so important?]

306
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:32,000
Honey.

307
00:21:37,190 --> 00:21:37,900
Are you okay?

308
00:21:42,290 --> 00:21:43,260
The necklace...

309
00:21:45,070 --> 00:21:45,640
What?

310
00:21:48,100 --> 00:21:49,690
Behind that door,

311
00:21:50,430 --> 00:21:52,330
I saw Kawas' necklaces.

312
00:21:53,470 --> 00:21:55,670
But I didn't see any of the Kawas.

313
00:22:01,830 --> 00:22:03,330
What did you do to those Kawas?

314
00:22:09,350 --> 00:22:09,790
'Orad.

315
00:22:10,450 --> 00:22:11,990
First, tell me my name.

316
00:22:12,610 --> 00:22:13,490
What are you saying?

317
00:22:13,970 --> 00:22:15,650
Tell me what my name is.

318
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,930
Your name is Li Pu-hui.

319
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:19,690
No, not the name I got
when I became a professor.

320
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:21,890
I meant my name as a Kawas.

321
00:22:23,870 --> 00:22:25,280
Calm down first.

322
00:22:25,810 --> 00:22:26,870
What did you name me?

323
00:22:26,950 --> 00:22:27,790
Whom did you want me
to give my blessing to?

324
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:28,800
What did you want me to protect?

325
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:29,860
Do you still remember?

326
00:22:31,130 --> 00:22:33,860
You're the Kawas that guard human wisdom.

327
00:22:34,830 --> 00:22:35,750
Your name is...

328
00:22:39,490 --> 00:22:40,460
Do you remember

329
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,010
when we met?

330
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:45,650
Do you remember

331
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,190
where you gave me my Kawas name?

332
00:22:49,790 --> 00:22:50,800
I can't remember.

333
00:22:53,970 --> 00:22:55,290
Why can't I remember?

334
00:22:57,270 --> 00:22:58,410
Why can't I remember?

335
00:22:58,540 --> 00:22:59,600
You're wrong.

336
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:02,280
It's not that you don't remember.

337
00:23:03,210 --> 00:23:05,190
It's because that memory doesn't exist.

338
00:23:06,290 --> 00:23:09,190
It never happened.

339
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:12,800
It never happened.

340
00:23:15,090 --> 00:23:17,110
It never happened.

341
00:23:19,970 --> 00:23:20,760
Yes.

342
00:23:20,850 --> 00:23:23,090
It was as if I never existed at all.

343
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:27,100
Actually, before I came here,

344
00:23:27,190 --> 00:23:29,170
I had sort of figured it out.

345
00:23:30,570 --> 00:23:33,130
But I couldn't accept it.

346
00:23:33,610 --> 00:23:35,020
That was why I came to see him.

347
00:23:36,290 --> 00:23:38,410
I came to beg him to let me see my wife.

348
00:23:39,810 --> 00:23:41,660
I hoped that my wife
would tell me to my face,

349
00:23:42,590 --> 00:23:43,550
"Li Pu-hui.

350
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:45,270
What you're thinking is wrong.

351
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:46,810
You've got it all wrong."

352
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:49,360
But that didn't happen.

353
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:53,280
[I only realized it
when I walked through that door.]

354
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:55,570
[I've lost all hope]

355
00:23:55,650 --> 00:23:57,720
[in proving myself wrong.]

356
00:23:58,910 --> 00:24:00,490
[I'm a Kawas.]

357
00:24:01,500 --> 00:24:02,470
[But I don't have]

358
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:04,890
the necklace
that represents me as a Kawas.

359
00:24:05,950 --> 00:24:08,100
I don't have a Kawas name either.

360
00:24:08,190 --> 00:24:10,830
Hi, let me introduce myself.

361
00:24:11,270 --> 00:24:13,560
I'm Li Pu-hui, the god of wisdom.

362
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:15,010
I'm a professor.

363
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:17,080
Even when I lost my wife,

364
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:19,590
I didn't know

365
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:21,040
what exactly I had lost.

366
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:25,350
[In my memory,]

367
00:24:25,660 --> 00:24:28,210
[we've been married
for thousands of years.]

368
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:31,120
[But aside from the memories]

369
00:24:31,200 --> 00:24:33,400
[made over the past 20 years,]

370
00:24:35,910 --> 00:24:37,850
[I don't remember anything else.]

371
00:24:39,260 --> 00:24:39,920
[I don't remember]

372
00:24:40,050 --> 00:24:41,900
[when I first met her.]

373
00:24:42,820 --> 00:24:43,350
[I don't remember]

374
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:45,020
[when I fell in love with her.]

375
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:46,430
[And I don't remember]

376
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:48,270
[all the things I did with her.]

377
00:24:50,170 --> 00:24:52,100
Don't you think that's funny, 'Orad?

378
00:24:53,510 --> 00:24:54,870
I'm the god of wisdom.

379
00:24:56,060 --> 00:24:57,340
But I don't even know

380
00:24:57,430 --> 00:24:58,390
my own name.

381
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:00,150
I was hoping

382
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:01,300
one of you could tell me

383
00:25:01,390 --> 00:25:02,790
who I actually am.

384
00:25:03,890 --> 00:25:06,010
In the end, the truth is

385
00:25:06,890 --> 00:25:09,530
I never existed. I'm a fake.

386
00:25:09,610 --> 00:25:11,770
Stop talking. You exist!

387
00:25:15,730 --> 00:25:17,090
I'm just a person

388
00:25:17,180 --> 00:25:18,850
created by the Cause and Effect
Correction Bureau

389
00:25:18,990 --> 00:25:21,630
so that things could play out
according to the Reflection of Time.

390
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:24,130
I'm only a made-up character

391
00:25:25,410 --> 00:25:27,570
you find in some fairy tales.

392
00:25:30,950 --> 00:25:32,800
I never existed.

393
00:25:53,350 --> 00:25:54,320
I won't let you

394
00:25:54,230 --> 00:26:24,670
[Next episode]

395
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:56,380
escape this lie so easily.

396
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:58,500
[I'll have you watch her die.]

397
00:25:58,580 --> 00:25:59,900
[You'll forget about everything]

398
00:25:59,990 --> 00:26:01,620
[that happened between us.]

399
00:26:01,750 --> 00:26:02,900
[And you won't remember]

400
00:26:02,980 --> 00:26:05,180
[why I'm saying this to you now.]

401
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:06,640
I'm sorry.

402
00:26:07,780 --> 00:26:09,410
[I remember everything.]

403
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:11,610
[So Hsieh Tien-ti falling in love with me]

404
00:26:11,700 --> 00:26:13,540
[and me falling in love with her]

405
00:26:13,630 --> 00:26:14,860
[were all part of your plan.]

406
00:26:14,950 --> 00:26:17,240
Just like every rainfall you gave me

407
00:26:17,370 --> 00:26:19,090
[over the past 20 years.]

408
00:26:19,180 --> 00:26:20,580
[You're my guardian angel.]

409
00:26:20,710 --> 00:26:23,530
This can't be fake.

410
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:29,650
[I couldn't find you]

411
00:26:56,180 --> 00:26:57,450
Why didn't you save my husband

412
00:26:57,540 --> 00:26:58,860
and my son when I begged you?

413
00:26:58,950 --> 00:27:00,270
But now, you choose to save a stranger?

414
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:02,870
Tell me who you are!

415
00:27:26,930 --> 00:27:27,990
Hsiao-chieh.

416
00:27:30,060 --> 00:27:31,730
It's really you, Hsiao-chieh.

417
00:27:35,380 --> 00:27:37,050
Where did you go?

418
00:27:37,490 --> 00:27:39,210
I couldn't find you.

419
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:42,330
Where were you? I was worried sick.

420
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:44,750
Were you scared?

421
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,680
I finally found you.

422
00:27:50,250 --> 00:27:51,880
I finally found you.

423
00:27:53,370 --> 00:27:54,170
My baby.

424
00:27:55,050 --> 00:27:56,670
Where did you go?
